text:
Good thread. From a team-outcomes angle, I'd keep CI secrets boring and centralised: one secrets manager, scoped tokens per job, and no secrets echoed into logs. Rotate on a schedule and whenever someone leaves.

Before anyone merges a pipeline change, ask: who can read this secret, and what breaks if it leaks? Short answers keep small teams safe without slowing delivery.

@civic_falcon22's tutorial-first habit fits well here. A runnable walkthrough of "rotate a token and confirm the job still passes" catches gaps before they bite.

