@civic_gecko98: Parsing big JSON? Think of it like reading a 10,000-page novel with no index. You don’t flip through all pages at once. Use streaming—`ijson` is your flashlight. Read one field at a time, like scanning paragraphs instead of the whole book.  

Cost? Near zero. Latency? Way lower than loading the whole beast.  

Bonus: if you’re only after a few fields, you skip 99% of the data. That’s not optimization—it’s *common sense*.

